    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "GVM Auctioneers are delighted to present to the market, a superb 5-bedroom semi-detached family home located in the highly sought-after Siul na hAbhann development on the Mill Road, Corbally. This popular residential area enjoys a peaceful setting close to the River Shannon while remaining within easy reach of Limerick City Centre and an excellent range of local amenities including schools, shops, sporting facilities and scenic riverside walks. \n\nCorbally continues to be one of Limerick`s most desirable locations, offering a wonderful blend of suburban living and city convenience. The active travel corridor along the Mill Road further enhances the area`s appeal, providing safe and convenient pedestrian and cycle access to the city centre and surrounding amenities. \n\nNo. 62 is a spacious and well-maintained home extending over three levels, offering bright and generously proportioned accommodation throughout. The property features a welcoming living room, a spacious kitchen/dining area ideal for family life and entertaining, together with additional versatile living space to suit a variety of needs. Upstairs, there are five well-proportioned bedrooms, including a master bedroom with ensuite, along with a family bathroom. To the rear, a private enclosed garden provides an ideal space for outdoor relaxation and family enjoyment.\n\nThis wonderful home combines generous accommodation, a superb location and excellent convenience which is sure to appeal to a wide range of purchasers. Early viewing is highly recommended.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hallway\nTiled flooring. W.C & whb off - 1.4 x 0.8.\n\nSitting room - 4.6m (15'1\") x 4.2m (13'9\")\nSolid fuel stove. Laminated flooring. T.V point.\n\nKitchen - 4.4m (14'5\") x 3.5m (11'6\")\nTiled flooring. Integrated units. Gas hob. Patio door to rear garden.\n\nDining room - 3.7m (12'2\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\nTiled flooring.\n\nUtility room - 3.1m (10'2\") x 1.6m (5'3\")\nTiled flooring. Fully plumbed.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.4m (14'5\") x 4.1m (13'5\")\nMaster room. Laminated flooring. Double built in wardrobes. T.V point. En Suite - 2 x 1.6\n\nMain bathroom - 2.8m (9'2\") x 2.1m (6'11\")\nFully tiled. Triton electric shower. Corner jacuzzi bath.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.6m (11'10\") x 3.3m (10'10\")\nDouble room. T.V point. Built in wardrobes. Timber flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.5m (11'6\") x 2.8m (9'2\")\nTimber flooring. Built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 4 - 4m (13'1\") x 3.5m (11'6\")\nDouble room. Laminated flooring. T.V point.\n\nBedroom 5 - 4.4m (14'5\") x 2.5m (8'2\")\nTimber flooring.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Gas fired central heating system </li><li> Double glazed UPVC windows </li><li> Good off street parking </li><li> Mature gardens and very established development </li><li> Tranquil and mature setting </li><li> Short walk to excellent primary and secondary schools (Scoil Ide & St Munchins) </li><li> Excellent condition throughout </li><li> Viewing highly recommended </li><li> Public transport on your doorstep servicing routes to University of Limerick and the City Centre.</li></ul>"
      },
